("api/bind-event" :names ("bind-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Register an observer without replacing any existing generic or control-specific registration. Signed 32-bit IDs are supported except -1 (reserved as native wxID_ANY; use NIL). LAST-ID requires ID and an ordered inclusive range. Observer bindings automatically Skip; contextual bindings start unskipped and control native Skip explicitly; relative callback order follows wxWidgets and is not a Lisp API guarantee. Failed registration releases temporary roots. Contextual access is limited to the innermost callback and expires at return, including on errors. A native entry-owned wxObject token adapter represents non-NIL user data without a Lisp/native pointer. EVENT-USER-DATA reads the per-binding value in snapshots/current contexts; there is no public mutation API for an existing association. ABI37 adds :NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGING/:NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGED notify-family observers/contexts. Only CHANGING veto affects navigation. Native page callbacks protect the originating book/ancestors and reject same-book recursive selection, modal and clipboard entry. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits. ABI39 tree selection changing/changed are native-only wxTreeEvent notify types. EVENT-TREE-ITEM captures canonical view identity, not frozen text/validity; same-tree writes and nested native loops defer until callback return. Native report-list and tree interaction kinds documented in REPORT-TREE-VIEWS are readonly notify payloads; expansion/collapse veto is available only for native before-events. No owned/synthetic/cloned views events." :position 28063)
("api/binding-active-p" :names ("binding-active-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query active-session registration and reap stale generic callback roots. Root pruning also runs at returned RUN/pump/notifying-setter boundaries and after explicit destruction. During a blocking RUN, native window closure may retain roots until a Lisp boundary or explicit unbinding. This does not change the control-specific callback-root contract." :position 36544)
("api/bitmap" :names ("bitmap") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Session-owned wxBitmap constructed from exactly one IMAGE or SOURCE; SOURCE copies BITMAP or native STATIC-BITMAP. Native backing pixel/logical/DIP size and scale remain distinct. SOURCE additionally accepts a BITMAP-TOGGLE-BUTTON for an owned copied native bitmap." :position 38312)
("api/bitmap-alive-p" :names ("bitmap-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query active-session bitmap validity; NIL after explicit disposal." :position 40122)
("api/bitmap-dip-size" :names ("bitmap-dip-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap GetDIPSize." :position 41250)
("api/bitmap-image" :names ("bitmap-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Convert native bitmap to image. Native alpha premultiplication/rounding can discard RGB under transparent pixels; this is not lossless archival conversion." :position 42315)
("api/bitmap-logical-size" :names ("bitmap-logical-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap GetLogicalSize; platform units differ from backing pixels." :position 43658)
("api/bitmap-scale-factor" :names ("bitmap-scale-factor") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap GetScaleFactor." :position 44846)
("api/bitmap-size" :names ("bitmap-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap dimensions; native static display readback may resample for DPI." :position 45942)
("api/bitmap-toggle-button" :names ("bitmap-toggle-button") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native wxBitmapToggleButton, not a text glyph. Inherits CHECKED-P/SETF and :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE. BITMAP-VALUE/SETF uses copied native values." :position 47112)
("api/bitmap-toggle-button-supported-p" :names ("bitmap-toggle-button-supported-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Report build/port availability; unavailable construction signals NATIVE-ERROR. Does not create a control or imply runtime verification on every port." :position 48810)
("api/bitmap-value" :names ("bitmap-value" "(setf bitmap-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read a newly owned native bitmap copy; caller disposes it. SETF copies source bitmap into the control. Source disposal does not invalidate the control. Bitmap-toggle receiver is availability-gated; copied allocation and all writes reject callbacks." :position 50135)
("api/button" :names ("button") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxButton with click handler support." :position 51905)
("api/calendar-date" :names ("calendar-date" "(setf calendar-date)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Local civil date without exposed time-of-day/timezone/Unix/universal-time. Gregorian leap/day/range validation; native construction/readback must preserve requested date. Native getter with no supported committed date signals NATIVE-ERROR." :position 53038)
