("api/cancel-ui-timer" :names ("cancel-ui-timer") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Stop native notifications, remove coalesced due work and release its root. Current periodic function can cancel itself; cannot interrupt an executing function." :position 59107)
("api/canvas-client-size" :names ("canvas-client-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Get native client size through ToDIP. Integer scaling may round by a pixel. Resize repaints retained data but does not rewrite the model; applications can rebuild geometry from this value. Reports retained native paint failure before returning." :position 60260)
("api/canvas-content" :names ("canvas-content" "(setf canvas-content)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Items are (:rect x y width height rgb), (:ellipse x y width height rgb), (:line x1 y1 x2 y2 rgb stroke-width), (:text x y string point-size rgb), or (:bitmap x y width height pixels). RGB bytes0..255, coordinates/endpoints ±10000, non-bitmap extents1..10000, line widths1..32, text6..72 points in native Swiss/sans family. Text is NUL/CR/LF-free, total65536 UTF-8 bytes; bitmaps1..256 per axis use exact simple RGB byte vectors, total2MiB. On-screen geometry uses DIP; no alpha/native resource handles. ABI60 adds :RGBA-BITMAP with copied straight RGBA bytes (4 per pixel), the same1..256 extent and2MiB aggregate scene cap; native alpha composition and screen DIP sizing apply." :position 61535)
