("api/delete-grid-rows" :names ("delete-grid-rows") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :position 96574)
("api/delete-item" :names ("delete-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete silently. Deleting the selected row clears selection; an earlier deletion shifts selected index down one, preserving the same item. No stable IDs or automatic domain-model updates. LIST-CONTROL deletes a stored report row only; virtual rows use item-count SETF." :position 97544)
("api/delete-list-column" :names ("delete-list-column") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete an existing column while item count0; return CONTROL." :position 98775)
("api/delete-notebook-page" :names ("delete-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete page and descendants; wrappers become invalid. Explicit deletion does not manufacture user-close veto/CLOSE/CLOSED sequence." :position 99547)
("api/delete-pending-events" :names ("delete-pending-events") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete queued native events without invoking callbacks; bindings and other handler queues remain intact. Synchronize wxApp pending-handler membership after deletion. Transferred input wrappers remain consumed; later queueing/posting still works." :position 101621)
("api/delete-stc-marker" :names ("delete-stc-marker") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native MarkerDelete. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :position 103444)
("api/delete-tree-item" :names ("delete-tree-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invalidate/delete whole subtree. Preserve an outside selection, otherwise choose surviving parent/root silently; deleting root leaves empty. Revision-prune invalid cached views." :position 104544)
("api/destroy-bitmap" :names ("destroy-bitmap") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Release native session-owned bitmap; displays retain independent native values." :position 105793)
("api/destroy-event" :names ("destroy-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Release this independent native event. Copies already queued/processing remain valid; repeated destruction rejects. Session cleanup releases undisposed owned events, even if the Lisp wrapper was collected." :position 106934)
("api/destroy-event-handler" :names ("destroy-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Destroy an owned standalone native handler. Outside callbacks deletion is immediate; during callbacks identity becomes invalid immediately and deletion is queued on the application after the current native dispatch stack. Repeated destruction is an error. Window and application identities are borrowed and reject this operation; use DESTROY-WINDOW for windows. Only session cleanup destroys the application. Destroying a linked standalone handler during a callback now rejects; outside callbacks native destruction splices reciprocal neighbors. Unlinked callback destruction retains existing deferral. Attached handlers are removed from their managed window before outside-callback deletion; linked/attached callback destruction rejects." :position 108126)
("api/destroy-image" :names ("destroy-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Release native session-owned image; stale/double disposal rejects." :position 110773)
("api/destroy-menu-resource" :names ("destroy-menu-resource") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete a resource through its native owner, invalidating descendants and wrapper handles. Menu/bar deletion removes it from its parent; frame lifetime also cleans remaining descendants. Structural callback/pump/RUN deletion rejects." :position 111883)
("api/destroy-window" :names ("destroy-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request destruction; first explicitly unbind handlers to release Lisp closures. Child handles become invalid when native destruction occurs. During native-to-Lisp callbacks the target becomes invalid immediately and native destruction is deferred using application CallAfter so dispatch/setter stacks can return safely. Generic bindings are reaped at Lisp boundaries; control-specific closures still require explicit unbinding or session cleanup." :position 113338)
("api/dialog" :names ("dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Shared bounded modal protocol and ordinary managed window lifetime." :position 115294)
("api/dialog-message" :names ("dialog-message") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read immutable message body. Title is separately mutable through DIALOG-TITLE; no message-body writer in this slice." :position 116775)
("api/dialog-modal-p" :names ("dialog-modal-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native modal state. False after END-MODAL is not permission to destroy the dialog/ancestor before SHOW-MODAL returns." :position 117779)
("api/dialog-selection" :names ("dialog-selection" "(setf dialog-selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write the single-choice selection index; NIL and out-of-range values reject. No item-list replacement API is added." :position 118738)
("api/dialog-selection-text" :names ("dialog-selection-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the last accepted native selection-string cache, not a string derived from the current selected index. SetSelection changes the index but GetStringSelection can remain empty until an actual OK-button transfer; a previous accepted cache can remain after index changes or raw END-MODAL. No cache synchronization is promised." :position 119955)
("api/dialog-title" :names ("dialog-title" "(setf dialog-title)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write native dialog title; scalar callback updates are allowed." :position 121371)
("api/dialog-value" :names ("dialog-value" "(setf dialog-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write native text-entry dialog value. Native GetValue is stored dialog data and need not expose live edit-buffer changes. SETF crosses the notifying callback boundary; callback conditions follow the existing Lisp condition protocol." :position 122430)
("api/directory-dialog" :names ("directory-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Uses wxGenericDirDialog with DIR_MUST_EXIST; never changes process working directory. Standard modal OK/Cancel, parent guards and eager native subclass hooks apply. Successful modal return validates existence again. No arbitrary native dialog adoption." :position 123894)
("api/directory-dialog-path" :names ("directory-dialog-path") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read-only selected directory path. Read after :OK; Cancel does not imply a selection change. Invalid/dead handles reject." :position 125257)
