("api/event" :names ("event") :kind :type :kind-name "Type" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read-only event snapshot: kind, receiving source handler/control, native event ID and process-local native type, copied text, checked state and selection. Data survives later callbacks and source destruction. Close snapshots capture CanVeto and GetVeto before this callback; they never reflect later context mutation. Registered names and family/integer data remain available in saved snapshots after session cleanup. Notify snapshots capture pre-callback veto capability/state independently of later Veto/Allow. Timestamp and native IsCommandEvent are copied before each callback; saved reads need no active session. Snapshot EVENT-USER-DATA captures the per-binding EQ Lisp reference before callback, independently of later unbinding. Mutable referent contents are not copied/frozen." :position 146390)
