("api/event-can-veto-p" :names ("event-can-veto-p" "(setf event-can-veto-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Snapshots read copied capability without a session. Current close contexts use CanVeto; current notify contexts always support Veto/Allow. Plain command contexts return NIL. Scope validation remains required for native access. Context SETF maps native SetCanVeto directly, including false to true. GetVeto hides a stored veto when CanVeto is false and reveals it again if re-enabled. Forced close starts false but explicit metadata mutation can affect native closing results; OS veto acceptance is not guaranteed." :position 155535)
("api/event-category" :names ("event-category") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read virtual GetEventCategory: current supported command/notify-derived classes report USER_INPUT and close/idle-family events report UI. Values are category flags, not event types/IDs/families; synthetic USER_INPUT is not proof of real user input. Snapshot values are captured before the callback." :position 158330)
("api/event-category-mask" :names ("event-category-mask") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Load the bridge and return its compiled wxEventCategory constant without initializing a GUI session. Combine with LOGIOR/test with LOGTEST. ALL can include implementation category bits and is not restricted to the public five-bit union." :position 160035)
("api/event-checked-p" :names ("event-checked-p" "(setf event-checked-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the kind-limited checked interpretation of native command integer. Live SETF writes SetInt(0/1) only for :TOGGLE/:MENU without calling a control setter. Raw EVENT-INTEGER can supply other nonzero checked values; earlier snapshots stay unchanged. Later native/user handlers can react to changed metadata; the entire dispatch is not guaranteed to leave controls unchanged. Native normal-menu commands may carry integer -1 and thus read checked true; this raw view does not classify a check item. :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE exposes read-only semantic checked metadata; raw integer edits remain observational, not control state changes." :position 161306)
