("api/event-command-p" :names ("event-command-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read captured/current native IsCommandEvent classification. No mutable classification or event replacement. Saved values remain independent of source lifetime." :position 164804)
("api/event-context" :names ("event-context") :kind :type :kind-name "Type" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "The context token is immutable; operations mutate the live native event only during its exact innermost callback. Nested contextual callbacks suspend outer access; nested observer/control callbacks also deny outer access. The outer context becomes usable again after nesting returns. Unbinding or deferred receiver disposal does not prematurely expire the running callback context. :CLOSE contexts allow checked veto access; command contexts do not have close-veto state." :position 166113)
("api/event-context-active-p" :names ("event-context-active-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Check scoped usability without dereferencing an expired pointer. Observer/control callbacks do not gain access to an enclosing context. The predicate does not assert receiver liveness and remains T during deferred receiver disposal until callback return." :position 168182)
