("api/event-handler" :names ("event-handler") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Concrete standalone wxEvtHandler wrapper and superclass of WINDOW. Standalone native objects are owned by the application session, explicitly destroyed or automatically freed at session cleanup, without a Lisp GC finalizer. Windows borrow their own native wxWindow base identity and retain window/parent lifetime. Neither case exposes an arbitrary GetEventHandler chain or permits user-supplied native handles. Standalone wrappers are now strongly canonicalized by session identity for EQ chain peer lookup; no new native ownership or finalizer is introduced. Managed window push leaves native ownership/session rooting unchanged; window destruction detaches handlers rather than deleting them." :position 185049)
