("api/event-stc-y" :names ("event-stc-y") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native client pixel Y for dwell start/end." :position 259687)
("api/event-text" :names ("event-text" "(setf event-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or copy native command string payload. Context/owned SETF uses explicit UTF-8 byte lengths, preserving embedded NULs. Saved snapshots stay immutable and retain their prior kind-specific payload interpretation. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits." :position 261251)
("api/event-time" :names ("event-time") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read captured/current native wxDateEvent time components independently of current control value; ignore date/milliseconds. Non-time or expired/outer contexts reject. Snapshot survives callback/session. No setter, owned/synthetic events or detached clones." :position 265711)
("api/event-timestamp" :names ("event-timestamp" "(setf event-timestamp)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied/current native timestamp, not necessarily Unix time. Negative values including -1 are valid. Synthetic events start at zero. Context SETF changes metadata only, not scheduling. Snapshots stay immutable and preserve pre-callback values." :position 267019)
("api/event-tree-item" :names ("event-tree-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Snapshot retains view identity, not live validity or frozen label. Non-tree snapshots return NIL; non-tree contexts reject. No owned-event method/setter; associated item can be invalidated later. Copy text while live if needed. New native activation/menu/expanding/expanded/collapsing/collapsed tree events retain checked borrowed same-tree item tokens." :position 269241)
("api/event-tree-position" :names ("event-tree-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh (x y) copied native tree-item-menu point, including native keyboard context requests. Also returns client coordinates for :TREE-BEGIN-DRAG." :position 270795)
("api/event-type" :names ("event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Look up a process-local native type ID. Twenty-two built-in kinds plus registered command/notify names are supported. Registry names are session-scoped; saved snapshot native IDs remain plain data after cleanup. Borrowed application handler access is supported; arbitrary native event-class binding and OS session delivery remains unverified." :position 271732)
("api/event-unicode-key" :names ("event-unicode-key") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Integer Unicode key value or NIL for WXK_NONE; not IME composition text." :position 273867)
("api/event-user-data" :names ("event-user-data") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the snapshot-captured or callback-frame-retained binding association. No deep copy: mutable referent contents remain ordinary Lisp state. Snapshot reads survive unbind/receiver/session cleanup. Current frames retain values across self/peer unbind and nested dispatch restores outer context identity." :position 275148)
("api/event-vetoed-p" :names ("event-vetoed-p" "(setf event-vetoed-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Snapshots retain pre-callback state. Close contexts use GetVeto / checked Veto(bool); notify contexts use NOT IsAllowed, Veto() for true, and Allow() for NIL. A close initialized non-vetoable rejects writes unless its current CanVeto flag was explicitly enabled through SETF EVENT-CAN-VETO-P. Plain command contexts reject live veto-state access. Snapshots stay immutable. Native GetVeto is CanVeto AND the stored veto bit; disabling capability hides the bit without clearing it." :position 276769)
("api/event-wheel-axis" :names ("event-wheel-axis") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary ":vertical or :horizontal." :position 279455)
