("api/event-wheel-rotation" :names ("event-wheel-rotation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Signed native wheel rotation, potentially finer than delta." :position 286697)
("api/file-dialog" :names ("file-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a generic single-file selection dialog. Directory/path accept strings or pathnames converted through native namestring; supplied directory must exist, empty directory lets native code use cwd. Path must be nonempty; filename is a string. Filters require nonempty description/pattern pairs and valid zero-based filter index. No change-directory flag, multiselect or external controls. Dialog browser actions such as New Directory can change the filesystem; selection does not perform file-content IO. True MUST-EXIST is rejected for :SAVE, and true OVERWRITE-PROMPT for :OPEN. Supplied path directories must exist." :position 287948)
("api/file-dialog-filter-index" :names ("file-dialog-filter-index" "(setf file-dialog-filter-index)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write one of the construction-time wildcard description/pattern pairs. Invalid index rejects. Filters do not prove current path acceptance." :position 290795)
("api/file-dialog-mode" :names ("file-dialog-mode") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read fixed single-file selection mode. Configured native UI validation differs from raw END-MODAL result assignment. Reader reflects the actual restored generic file flags, including the macOS overlap repair, rather than merely echoing a Lisp requested-mode slot." :position 292218)
("api/file-dialog-path" :names ("file-dialog-path" "(setf file-dialog-path)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write current single-file path. This is not acceptance, file existence, overwrite confirmation or successful content IO. A raw END-MODAL :OK bypasses button validation/transfer, must-exist and overwrite enforcement. Native property changes can open internal prompts and use the guarded prompt workflow." :position 293491)
("api/fill-stc-indicator-range" :names ("fill-stc-indicator-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native GetLength, IndicatorFillRange. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :position 295304)
("api/fit-scroll-content" :names ("fit-scroll-content") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Layout/FitInside/Layout refreshes virtual extent from max(client,sizer minimum), without resizing frame. Requires own sizer and supported content extent; no callback mutation." :position 296470)
("api/flush-clipboard" :names ("flush-clipboard") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Best-effort persistence after exit, on the standard clipboard. Does not set clipboard contents. A false native Flush result is normal; open/session failures signal NATIVE-ERROR." :position 297650)
("api/focus-window" :names ("focus-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request native SetFocus, or SetFocusFromKbd for a keyboard-origin request. Containers can delegate focus to children; keyboard focus can select text according to the native control." :position 298897)
