("api/handler-alive-p" :names ("handler-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Observe native lifetime without dereferencing dead windows. Native weak tracking makes window destruction safe even with event processing disabled. A failed/uninitialized Lisp wrapper has no handle and signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup invalidates every identity; outside a session this query signals NATIVE-ERROR." :position 329221)
("api/handler-enabled-p" :names ("handler-enabled-p" "(setf handler-enabled-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or write the native wxEvtHandler event-processing flag. Separate from window ENABLED-P/input state: disabled handlers can skip callbacks without greying the control. Native propagation rules still apply. Scoped contexts support Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto; arbitrary pushed handlers remain unbound. In standalone chains this affects only the node itself, not processing by following nodes." :position 331203)
("api/handler-unlinked-p" :names ("handler-unlinked-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native IsUnlinked without changing native ownership or queue membership. An unlinked wrapper remains strongly registered and its native object remains session-owned until explicit destruction or cleanup." :position 333541)
("api/hide-grid-cell-edit-control" :names ("hide-grid-cell-edit-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :position 334796)
("api/hide-stc-lines" :names ("hide-stc-lines") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native HideLines. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :position 335830)
