("api/on-click" :names ("on-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :CLICK snapshots with no payload. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 468062)
("api/on-selection" :names ("on-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :SELECTION snapshots with selected index or NIL. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index." :position 469900)
("api/on-text-change" :names ("on-text-change") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TEXT-CHANGE snapshots with copied text. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 472130)
("api/on-toggle" :names ("on-toggle") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TOGGLE snapshots with boolean state. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 473955)
("api/owned-event" :names ("owned-event") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed CLOS construction supports subclasses, slot initargs, defaults and AFTER hooks. Native origin is NIL. Mixed ancestry with EVENT-HANDLER/window is invalid. Explicit destruction or session cleanup owns deletion; there is no GC finalizer." :position 475748)
("api/panel" :names ("panel") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for a child wxPanel." :position 477903)
("api/pending-events-p" :names ("pending-events-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents across the current application. Does not report OS input, idle work or timers that have not queued an event. It is an observation, not a guarantee about the next dispatch. Safe to query during callbacks." :position 478968)
("api/pop-event-handler" :names ("pop-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach the top entry. Default preserves native owned registry/root; DELETE true releases bridge ownership before native PopEventHandler deletion and clears canonical roots/bindings. Empty stacks reject instead of invoking native assertions." :position 480076)
("api/popup-choice" :names ("popup-choice") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously display a temporary native context menu. Labels and flags are copied; the native menu is destroyed before returning. No menu resource escapes. Use :separator between command groups; separators are disabled, count in the returned zero-based indexes and 16-entry limit, and cannot lead, trail or be consecutive." :position 482039)
("api/position-panel" :names ("position-panel") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Set panel geometry, lay out its children and raise above siblings, for in-window overlays. Use FROM-DIP when starting from DIP sizes." :position 483617)
("api/post-event" :names ("post-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post an independent detached copy with wxPostEvent/AddPendingEvent; attach the receiver as copy origin. Input stays live/unchanged and may be destroyed or changed immediately. Delivery is asynchronous in the managed GUI session." :position 484529)
("api/previous-handler" :names ("previous-handler" "(setf previous-handler)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native previous link. SETF mirrors NEXT-HANDLER, joining vacant source-previous/peer-next endpoints reciprocally or detaching one edge for NIL. Self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation; an existing reciprocal pair is idempotent." :position 486259)
("api/process-event" :names ("process-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously dispatch a fresh owned synthetic event through ProcessEvent, copy final veto state and then delete the event. Observer callbacks may run while handled-p is NIL because they Skip; native consumption/default handling determines the first result. Final veto is independent of handled-p and may be true from initial VETOED-P even without a matching handler. Close dispatch can run frame defaults. Callback errors re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary; handled nested errors do not stop RUN. No final values are returned when a condition escapes, and earlier callback mutations are not rolled back. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 488404)
("api/process-event-locally" :names ("process-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously process an independent detached copy with ProcessEventLocally, including local pre-processing and native chained handlers, without normal outer global-filter/parent/application fallback. Source remains live/unchanged. Observer delivery can return handled NIL; final veto is independent. Native local static/default handlers may still execute, including frame-close behavior; local processing is not observer-only or a no-default-action mode." :position 492949)
("api/process-events" :names ("process-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Yield to GUI events and process idle work without waiting for new input; re-signal callback errors after returning from native polling." :position 495259)
("api/process-pending-events" :names ("process-pending-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Dispatch queued wx events for all pending handlers of the bridge application via ProcessPendingEvents. Does not yield to OS input or run ProcessIdle. Does not wait for new events; callback duration and continuously requeued work may delay return. Callback conditions are contained at the native boundary and re-signaled afterwards." :position 496265)
("api/process-window-event" :names ("process-window-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Process a detached copy through native GetEventHandler stack routing, window and normal parent/application fallback. Source remains alive/unchanged; copy origin is WINDOW and callback source can be a pushed handler. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary." :position 497900)
("api/process-window-event-locally" :names ("process-window-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Search the window and its pushed handlers with local pre-processing/validators, without normal upward window propagation. Process an independent detached copy with receiver-window origin and unchanged source. Observer delivery may still return handled NIL. Native local static/default handlers can still run, including frame-close behavior; local routing is not observer-only." :position 499851)
("api/pulse-gauge" :names ("pulse-gauge") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request platform-native indeterminate progress. Call periodically while keeping the GUI event loop responsive. Visual animation and value readings vary by platform; no timer, worker dispatch or completion event is provided. SETF GAUGE-VALUE restores determinate mode." :position 502018)
("api/push-event-handler" :names ("push-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Push above the existing stack top while keeping native ownership in the bridge registry. Reject linked/attached or borrowed window/app peers, active session bindings and queued session events before mutation." :position 503305)
("api/queue-click" :names ("queue-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post a button click for later dispatch. It uses the handler registered at dispatch time, including any replacement." :position 505174)
("api/queue-event" :names ("queue-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Queue a copied synthetic event: wxCommandEvent for seven command kinds, wxCloseEvent for close/session kinds and wxIdleEvent for :IDLE. Ordinary control properties are not changed directly. A queued close on a frame may run its native default closing action; use CLOSE-WINDOW for a synchronous acceptance result. Explicit UTF-8 lengths preserve text. Close events take no command payload, may be vetoable or non-vetoable, and do not normally propagate to parents. Registry types create wxCommandEvent or wxNotifyEvent according to their declared family. Initial veto applies only to custom notify types. Queuing offers no final veto/handled result; use PROCESS-EVENT when a synchronous decision is required. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 506149)
("api/queue-thread-event" :names ("queue-thread-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Worker-safe wxThreadEvent delivery. Copies bytes before return and never invokes Lisp GUI callbacks on the posting thread. GUI BIND-EVENT :THREAD receives copied EVENT-TEXT in a base-family snapshot/current context. Queue acceptance does not guarantee callback delivery. The packet stores an independently owned native wxThreadEvent string through SetString; all worker temporary aliases die before publication. GetString and inherited native Clone retain native string semantics; public owned-event cloning remains unsupported." :position 511577)
("api/radio-box" :names ("radio-box") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods." :position 513898)
("api/realize-toolbar" :names ("realize-toolbar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator." :position 515142)
("api/refresh-list-items" :names ("refresh-list-items") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invalidate inclusive native row range; provider data remains application-owned. Return CONTROL." :position 516069)
("api/register-event-type" :names ("register-event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Allocate a process-local native event type and map NAME in the active session. Duplicate names, built-ins and unsupported families are rejected before registration. Names cannot be unregistered or replaced during this session. Registrations are session-wide metadata, not rolled back when an unrelated resource initializer fails. Native type IDs are not stable across processes." :position 516921)
("api/remove-event-handler" :names ("remove-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Preflight membership and detach without deletion. A live detached handler or handler belonging to another window returns NIL unchanged; only present entries reach native RemoveEventHandler, avoiding its absent-entry assertion." :position 518663)
("api/remove-notebook-page" :names ("remove-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach/hide without deletion or reparenting. Returned panel can be reinserted or explicitly destroyed, but remains a native child and dies with book." :position 520600)
("api/replace-splitter-pane" :names ("replace-splitter-pane") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace an attached pane, explicitly hide the old pane and show the new one." :position 522727)
("api/replace-stc-range" :names ("replace-stc-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace a native byte range; read-only rejects. Native modifications notify under existing guards; no general rollback after native callback errors." :position 523891)
("api/replace-text" :names ("replace-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace half-open native [FROM,TO) with VALUE using native Replace and text-change notification. Equal endpoints insert, empty VALUE removes. Mutation may precede a callback condition rethrow; handled conditions permit recovery. Exact no-op event counts, caret/selection and undo effects are port-specific." :position 525504)
("api/reset-grid-cell-editor" :names ("reset-grid-cell-editor") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :position 526957)
("api/resplit-window" :names ("resplit-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Attach second pane using current orientation/requested sash geometry. Native geometry can clamp." :position 527972)
("api/resume-event-propagation" :names ("resume-event-propagation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Restore the native propagation level without changing Skip. Zero is allowed and keeps propagation stopped. Invalid LEVEL signals TYPE-ERROR; expired contexts reject native access." :position 529154)
("api/return-to-application-repl" :names ("return-to-application-repl") :kind :restart :kind-name "Restart" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Abandon the failing REPL evaluation or callback operation using the active debugger restart." :position 530918)
("api/run" :names ("run") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Block until STOP or the last top-level frame closes. Callback errors are re-signaled after returning from native code." :position 531729)
("api/run-web-script" :names ("run-web-script") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Asynchronously evaluates JavaScript. JSON-fragment success (undefined maps to null), native error or non-serializable result failure arrives through :web-script-result. Results over1MiB become an error. Ticket retires before event callbacks. Messages posted to window.webkit.messageHandlers.wxlambda.postMessage(value) arrive as JSON via :web-message; at most256 queued messages, each up to1MiB, excess dropped. Owner teardown drops late completions. Queued immutable command snapshots: :web-message text is JSON (including quoted strings); :web-script-result text is JSON on success or an error description on failure, EVENT-INTEGER is1/0 and EVENT-EXTRA-LONG is the request ticket; :web-loaded text is native URL and :web-error text is native error description. BIND-EVENT supports scoped contexts/Skip/propagation but payload SETF rejects. Async delivery occurs through normal GUI polling/RUN, never directly from an Objective-C completion. Native loaded/error events can reflect prior/subframe navigation; no exact per-navigation correlation or veto API." :position 532640)
("api/save-canvas-image" :names ("save-canvas-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Render same retained scene into private RGB24 bitmap and PNG. Export coordinates are pixels, one scene unit per pixel with clipping, not model scaling; fonts keep native point-size metrics. Internal PNG handler does not alter global registry. Existing target is overwritten; encoding is staged before open, but write/flush/close failure can leave partial output and is not atomic replacement." :position 536395)
("api/save-grid-edit-control-value" :names ("save-grid-edit-control-value") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :position 538350)
("api/save-image" :names ("save-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Encode via native PNG handler and write/flush/close the local native pathname. Existing output may be overwritten; failure may leave a partial file." :position 539388)
